A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="X" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="WO-1998053982-A1" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>WO</country><doc-number>1998053982</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIMOTO YUKITANE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIDO TOSHIHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMOTO, YUKITANE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIDO, TOSHIHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TORAY INDUSTRIES, INC.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KIMOTO YUKITANE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KONDO TOSHIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SEKIDO TOSHIHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KIMOTO, YUKITANE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KONDO, TOSHIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SEKIDO, TOSHIHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An FRP structure body having a plurality of sheets of core material laminated in a thickness direction and an FRP skin layer disposed on at least one side of the core material; an FRP structure body comprising a pair of spaced-apart sheets, at least one sheet containing FRP, and a seamless, enclosed hollow core material contained in the space; production methods for these FRP structure bodies; and a method of repairing an FRP structure body, wherein, when a portion not impregnated with resin is found on the surface of the body, the non-impregnated portion is entirely covered with a bag base material, the inside covered with the bag base material is vacuumized and resin is injected into the inside for impregnating into the non-resin-impregnated portion of a reinforcing fiber base material. A multiple-layer core structure allows an easy formation of a comparatively large FRP structure body having curved surfaces. An FRP structure body containing a seamless, enclosed hollow core material has lightweight and high-strength features and can be easily formed by a vacuum RTM method. The above repairing method permits an easy, low-cost repairing without sacrifice in strength to thereby reduce the production costs of an FRP structure body.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne une structure en stratifié plastique renforcé (SPR) comprenant une pluralité de feuilles stratifiées dans le sens de l'épaisseur et une couche de surface dans le même matériau disposée sur au moins su un côté du matériau central. L'invention concerne également une structure SPR comprenant une paire de feuilles espacées l'une de l'autre, au moins une feuille du SPR et un matériau central, creux, sans raccord, dans l'espace ainsi matérialisé. Par ailleurs, cette invention concerne une méthode de réparation d'une structure SPR. Selon cette méthode, une partie non imprégnée de résine  présente sur la surface de la structure est entièrement recouverte d'une treillis. Après mise sous vide de l'intérieur, qui est également recouvert d'un treillis, on y injecte une résine qui va imprégner la partie non imprégnée du matériau en fibre de renforcement. Une structure centrale multicouche facilite la formation d'une structure SPR renforcé de relativement grande taille aux surfaces incurvées. La structure SPR à matériau central creux, sans raccord, se caractérise par sa légèreté et sa grande robustesse, et peut être façonnée facilement au moyen d'une technique de moulage par transfert de résine. La méthode de réparation susmentionnée est simple et peu coûteuse, sans compromis au niveau de la robustesse, ce qui permet de réduire les coûts de production des structures en stratifié plastique renforcé (SPR).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>